BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 333.77 Tm (The closing desk is where creative files die first. Caleb Christopher recorded a cold call to a title company in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.55 Tm (Wisconsin, a state where he had not worked yet. The escrow staffer asked whether the deal was ultimately a cash) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 303.32 Tm (transaction. Caleb explained there might be no cash to the seller and that it was not an assumption, only continued) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.10 Tm (payment on behalf of the mortgagor. After checking with the owner, the answer was 'we're gonna pass') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.87 Tm ([BBTWC2u7edM @ 00:02:20]. Scott Horne sees the same reflex everywhere. New investors default to the title) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.65 Tm (company they know, and title company ABC looks at the sub-to and says 'Yeah, we can't do this' [fNubolIgxnE @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 242.42 Tm (00:08:58]. He adds that many title companies claim to understand creative deals and really do not. By his count only) Tj ET
