BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 151.07 Tm (The wrap carries traps that detonate after closing. Rucker warns that the due-on-sale clause gives the bank a technical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 135.85 Tm (right to call the note. Banks usually do not act while payments arrive on time, but they absolutely can, so the buyer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 120.62 Tm (must be ready to refinance and pay off the underlying loan [4coBBRVrtIA @ 00:03:56]. He flags a self-inflicted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 105.40 Tm (wound as well. Sellers who cancel the old insurance policy to save money can make the old bank panic and move) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 90.17 Tm (toward foreclosure. His fix is double coverage: the original policy stays in place and the buyer buys a new one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 74.95 Tm ([4coBBRVrtIA @ 00:04:32]. Rucker adds that under Texas law, a missed 7-day underlying-lien notice hands the buyer) Tj ET
