BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (is simple: due on the 1st, late on the 2nd, a 10-day grace period, and a late charge starting day 11. A late notice plus) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (email, text, and call go out after the grace period; by the 20th the investor is told and urged to call the borrower, and in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (Texas the recommended law firm sends the initial foreclosure notice on the 20th so months of nonpayment do not pile) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (up [adTW0EyLeRk @ 00:19:19]. Escrow shortfalls against an underlying lender come out of the investor's principal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (and interest, overages are held until the annual analysis, and borrowers cure shortages in a lump sum or over 12) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (months. On the collection side, FIXnotes pairs one RESPA hello letter with one attorney letter that routes callers to a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (web form or straight to a cell phone [5H6jVWw2QK0 @ 00:01:11].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (Pricing is where operators get nickel-and-dimed. FIXnotes puts full-service collections at about $90 per loan per month) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (plus a contingency fee and says no servicer at that price produced satisfying results; client-managed servicing at $30 is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (standard, with bare-bones shops as low as $15, and the BSI itemized fee menu is the benchmark for comparing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (boarding, deboarding, bankruptcy, and loss mitigation charges [5H6jVWw2QK0 @ 00:04:06]. Rick of Paperstac sees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (performing servicing from $10 to $35, warns that $35 on a $200 payment eats nearly 25% of revenue, and flags) Tj ET
