BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 369.65 Tm (collecting principal, interest, taxes and insurance as one payment and keeping the escrow, which Nathan calls a big) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 354.42 Tm (no-no because that is the borrower's money held for them [uKK5_EVlvus @ 00:20:37]. The contract for deed was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 339.20 Tm (never recorded, which Nathan says means it does not exist in the judicial system, so there is nothing to enforce when) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 323.97 Tm (payments stop, and the last three months of payments had already been missed, making it a non-performing note on top) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 308.75 Tm (of everything else. Nathan told the seller to tune it up first; the seller never fixed it, and the deal died [uKK5_EVlvus @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 293.52 Tm (00:22:27].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 278.30 Tm (When paper like that reaches a servicer, the reversal comes fast. Sohail sees at least a couple of non-compliant notes a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 263.07 Tm (week; the blatantly out-of-compliance ones get rejected or sent back for the lender to reclose with Provident's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 247.85 Tm (corrections, and lenders who refuse simply cannot board, because the servicer will not absorb the reputational risk of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 232.62 Tm (borrower who sues everybody involved [uKK5_EVlvus @ 00:07:44]. In court the downside is worse: best case the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 217.40 Tm (documents get corrected, worst case a judge nullifies the contract with a rescission, the lender refunds everything the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 202.17 Tm (borrower paid over, say, five years, and then waits for the property to be vacated; on a wrap, most of those proceeds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 186.95 Tm (already went to the underlying note [uKK5_EVlvus @ 00:13:40]. The panel also kills the pre-signed deed in lieu and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 171.72 Tm (the clause making a note null and void at 30 days in arrears, because a borrower cannot be bound in advance to hand) Tj ET
